(3628765, 503282, 67258, '<td valign="top">Alex, this really is quite exquisite, and a very worthy ribbon winner.<br/>I have just looked at my statistically favourite photographers ranking and discover that in the 28 challenges on which I have voted and you have enetered, my average score for you is 7.6071 - that is quite some feat!</td>', 'Alex, this really is quite exquisite, and a very worthy ribbon winner.I have just looked at my statistically favourite photographers ranking and discover that in the 28 challenges on which I have voted and you have enetered, my average score for you is 7.6071 - that is quite some feat!', '2007-05-08 13:56:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(3628769, 503265, 1024, '<td valign="top">A lot of people on DPC are not fond of woodies.  I do not know why...<br/> <br/>I loved the cobwebs in this image but it does not really speak to me if you know what I mean.  It is missing the "wow" factor.</td>', 'A lot of people on DPC are not fond of woodies.  I do not know why... I loved the cobwebs in this image but it does not really speak to me if you know what I mean.  It is missing the "wow" factor.', '2007-05-08 13:58:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(3628781, 503464, 63495, '<td valign="top">Kelly i really like the angle. To makeup is cool, you must be good at post editing to apply makeup like that</td>', 'Kelly i really like the angle. To makeup is cool, you must be good at post editing to apply makeup like that', '2007-05-08 14:01:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(3628797, 503828, 15291, '<td valign="top">Hi Lorrie,<br/>         Fantastic image. However I did notice two things here that caught my eye. The hinge on the chest is a little distracting &amp; the burning around the eyes (ring) just don''t seem normal. Other then that why mess with perfection wonderful image.</td>', 'Hi Lorrie,         Fantastic image. However I did notice two things here that caught my eye. The hinge on the chest is a little distracting & the burning around the eyes (ring) just don''t seem normal. Other then that why mess with perfection wonderful image.', '2007-05-08 14:10:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(3628799, 500041, 56539, '<td valign="top">You are one of the main people that makes me love Expert Editing and get my vote to make it an integral part of the challenges. Your knowledge of Photoshop is phenomenal and you put it to good use.  I only wish that I could be half as good as you.  Great image!  Keep it up---please!</td>', 'You are one of the main people that makes me love Expert Editing and get my vote to make it an integral part of the challenges. Your knowledge of Photoshop is phenomenal and you put it to good use.  I only wish that I could be half as good as you.  Great image!  Keep it up---please!', '2007-05-08 14:11:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(3628805, 501983, 5112, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club<br/> <br/>I remember seeing this image during the voting stage.  My first thought was, "Good candid!"  I love the smile, it is so engaging, it is all over his face.  The B/W treatment suits the image well.  I gave it a 7.<br/> <br/>That said, the main "distractions" are the strings in front of the face, and the busy background.  The background is part of the story, but it is slightly blurred, so it sort becomes something where you don''t know: is it a background, or is it part of the story?  The strings, they actually look good in front of his face, but at first glance they are a bit put-offy.  In a challenge, most people only look at each image for a few seconds.  If something looks odd, they will vote the image a lower score.  The strings in front of the face look a bit odd.<br/> <br/>As for technicals, I see no problems.  The exposure/post-processing are very good.<br/> <br/>I hope this helps.  If I can be of further help, please let me know.<br/> <br/>~Ursula</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club I remember seeing this image during the voting stage.  My first thought was, "Good candid!"  I love the smile, it is so engaging, it is all over his face.  The B/W treatment suits the image well.  I gave it a 7. That said, the main "distractions" are the strings in front of the face, and the busy background.  The background is part of the story, but it is slightly blurred, so it sort becomes something where you don''t know: is it a background, or is it part of the story?  The strings, they actually look good in front of his face, but at first glance they are a bit put-offy.  In a challenge, most people only look at each image for a few seconds.  If something looks odd, they will vote the image a lower score.  The strings in front of the face look a bit odd. As for technicals, I see no problems.  The exposure/post-processing are very good. I hope this helps.  If I can be of further help, please let me know. ~Ursula', '2007-05-08 14:12:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(3628812, 503265, 67258, '<td valign="top">I am not a woody-hater as such, but in this case they have turned what I thought a rather good study of something mundane into a kitsch creation that takes away from the quality of the original image.  On a (slightly) less subjective, and more technical, level, the light on the woodies just doesn''t seem quite right when compared to the placement of the light source; the focus on the woodies seems quite soft compared to that of the light and it''s fittings; and the composition seems not quite right - I would have preferred to see all of the woody on the right, stretching out and reaching for the light, hoverring in the air.  Hope this helps a little.</td>', 'I am not a woody-hater as such, but in this case they have turned what I thought a rather good study of something mundane into a kitsch creation that takes away from the quality of the original image.  On a (slightly) less subjective, and more technical, level, the light on the woodies just doesn''t seem quite right when compared to the placement of the light source; the focus on the woodies seems quite soft compared to that of the light and it''s fittings; and the composition seems not quite right - I would have preferred to see all of the woody on the right, stretching out and reaching for the light, hoverring in the air.  Hope this helps a little.', '2007-05-08 14:14:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(3628821, 504057, 62318, '<td valign="top">Nice composition and complimentary colors. A nice angle for the pier. I like the simplicity of the photo. Nice work.</td>', 'Nice composition and complimentary colors. A nice angle for the pier. I like the simplicity of the photo. Nice work.', '2007-05-08 14:15:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(3628828, 503394, 62318, '<td valign="top">Nice detail in the fur. The lighting is actually pretty good and well as the pose of the bird. A good nature shot.</td>', 'Nice detail in the fur. The lighting is actually pretty good and well as the pose of the bird. A good nature shot.', '2007-05-08 14:17:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(3628829, 504057, 67152, '<td valign="top">simply gorgeous - love the colors, love the light bursts, love the composition, love the quietness - would have given it at least an 8 had I got around to voting on the whole challenge (I only made it about 40% through...)</td>', 'simply gorgeous - love the colors, love the light bursts, love the composition, love the quietness - would have given it at least an 8 had I got around to voting on the whole challenge (I only made it about 40% through...)', '2007-05-08 14:17:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(3628836, 505471, 62318, '<td valign="top">Nice lines and a terrific idea to incorporate a person to bring some interest to the photo. I really like the movement created here, it helps with the entire image. Nice lighting and post work.</td>', 'Nice lines and a terrific idea to incorporate a person to bring some interest to the photo. I really like the movement created here, it helps with the entire image. Nice lighting and post work.', '2007-05-08 14:18:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(3628840, 493871, 23478, '<td valign="top">Great photo, great title.  congratulations on your top ten finish!</td>', 'Great photo, great title.  congratulations on your top ten finish!', '2007-05-08 14:19:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(3628842, 505169, 5112, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/>Interesting idea, "competing against yourself", and you went to a lot of trouble to edit this image.<br/> <br/><b>Strong points:</b>  The kid looks great, good smile, great postures.  The blurred background has just enough detail to give context without becoming intrussive.  The colours are gentle and good to look at.  The composition is fine.<br/> <br/><b>Possible weaknesses:</b>  The second pasted in shot (your son on the right) looks very much pasted in.  It is not organic with the field, it looks like he''s floating there, not really part of the image.  However, you did a great job of editing out the other people you mention in your notes.<br/> <br/><b>Overall:</b>  This is two nice images of your son playing soccer, but as a composite it needs more work to really work.  Also, even though the image might mean a lot to you and your son, usually family pictures do not have a strong meaning to other viewers, especially viewers who will spend only a couple seconds voting on each image.<br/> <br/>I hope this helps.  If I can be of further help, please let me know.<br/> <br/>~Ursula<br/> <br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club  Interesting idea, "competing against yourself", and you went to a lot of trouble to edit this image. Strong points:  The kid looks great, good smile, great postures.  The blurred background has just enough detail to give context without becoming intrussive.  The colours are gentle and good to look at.  The composition is fine. Possible weaknesses:  The second pasted in shot (your son on the right) looks very much pasted in.  It is not organic with the field, it looks like he''s floating there, not really part of the image.  However, you did a great job of editing out the other people you mention in your notes. Overall:  This is two nice images of your son playing soccer, but as a composite it needs more work to really work.  Also, even though the image might mean a lot to you and your son, usually family pictures do not have a strong meaning to other viewers, especially viewers who will spend only a couple seconds voting on each image. I hope this helps.  If I can be of further help, please let me know. ~Ursula ', '2007-05-08 14:20:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(3628851, 504647, 56539, '<td valign="top">Pay no attention to the well-known chronic complainers.  Your work is excellent.  A 10 from me and well deserved.</td>', 'Pay no attention to the well-known chronic complainers.  Your work is excellent.  A 10 from me and well deserved.', '2007-05-08 14:21:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(3628853, 505659, 62318, '<td valign="top">I like how all the elements work in the frame. I like how the lighting/coloring is even with all the elements you combined. I would not have known it was the Wright Flyer on the left without the title (I thought it was some sort of ancient symbolism). A nice use of the expert rules.</td>', 'I like how all the elements work in the frame. I like how the lighting/coloring is even with all the elements you combined. I would not have known it was the Wright Flyer on the left without the title (I thought it was some sort of ancient symbolism). A nice use of the expert rules.', '2007-05-08 14:21:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(3628870, 505454, 15291, '<td valign="top">Moring Julie,<br/>            I think you picked the wrong person for this image. Her skin tone is to pale. The eyes are over done in relation to her skin tone. The iris blue halo is also a bit of a distraction. Over all I must say this image is very eary looks as if she has died with her eyes open.</td>', 'Moring Julie,            I think you picked the wrong person for this image. Her skin tone is to pale. The eyes are over done in relation to her skin tone. The iris blue halo is also a bit of a distraction. Over all I must say this image is very eary looks as if she has died with her eyes open.', '2007-05-08 14:26:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(3628872, 504237, 30214, '<td valign="top">wonderful image, congrats!</td>', 'wonderful image, congrats!', '2007-05-08 14:26:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(3628891, 505253, 23478, '<td valign="top">Very cool image and like you mentioned, not as powerful as the triptych.  I love the colors of the other image and the way that it flows also.  <br/> <br/>Congrats on your top 20 finish.</td>', 'Very cool image and like you mentioned, not as powerful as the triptych.  I love the colors of the other image and the way that it flows also.   Congrats on your top 20 finish.', '2007-05-08 14:29:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(3628911, 505016, 23478, '<td valign="top">great shot and an excellent use of B&amp;W!</td>', 'great shot and an excellent use of B&W!', '2007-05-08 14:33:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(3628923, 504935, 61651, '<td valign="top">Nice crisp shot - it''s likely a lot of viewers just didn''t find anything interesting in the subject matter, which contributed to your middle-of-the-road scores.  I wonder how it would look if you took the shot at a slightly different angle, positioned from more to the left, so you can see more of the side of the car as well as the front - don''t know if it would be better/worse/same, just wondering. :)</td>', 'Nice crisp shot - it''s likely a lot of viewers just didn''t find anything interesting in the subject matter, which contributed to your middle-of-the-road scores.  I wonder how it would look if you took the shot at a slightly different angle, positioned from more to the left, so you can see more of the side of the car as well as the front - don''t know if it would be better/worse/same, just wondering. :)', '2007-05-08 14:36:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(3628930, 504415, 15291, '<td valign="top">Hello Al,<br/>        Nice image. A few things I would like to point here are. The tree or bush in the lower right hand corner is a little distracting keeps pulling my eye. I would have liked to see the full tree on your main subject, just a little bother some having the very top abrutly cut off, and a little more detail in the rocks would have done well here. I do like the placement of all your elements also the contrasting scheme is well done.</td>', 'Hello Al,        Nice image. A few things I would like to point here are. The tree or bush in the lower right hand corner is a little distracting keeps pulling my eye. I would have liked to see the full tree on your main subject, just a little bother some having the very top abrutly cut off, and a little more detail in the rocks would have done well here. I do like the placement of all your elements also the contrasting scheme is well done.', '2007-05-08 14:38:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(3628936, 504935, 40973, '<td valign="top">I did not vote in the free study and I know absolutely nothing about cars. It did get an average vote of 6.5 from commenters who were interested in the subject. Perhaps if you had more of the car and less of the surroundings in the photo and severely grunged it up it would have been noticed a bit more. Particularly if you had a beautiful young woman on the hood.</td>', 'I did not vote in the free study and I know absolutely nothing about cars. It did get an average vote of 6.5 from commenters who were interested in the subject. Perhaps if you had more of the car and less of the surroundings in the photo and severely grunged it up it would have been noticed a bit more. Particularly if you had a beautiful young woman on the hood.', '2007-05-08 14:41:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(3628940, 505484, 5112, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club<br/> <br/>Strong points:  The light.  The light is very beautiful in this image, it''s what makes the image.<br/> <br/>Possible weaknesses:  It''s not all that interesting of a place (for a picture in a challenge I mean).<br/> <br/>Overall, I think this is a beautiful image, because of the light, but outside of that there isn''t much to hold anyone (except if you know the place and want to remember the good times you had there).  It''s a real pity you didn''t get more comments.  I don''t think the "distractions" are an issue here, but it is possible that a slightly different crop (or different position to make the image) would help.<br/> <br/>As for the post-processing, I think it is really quite adequate for the picture.  One possibility would be to intensify the red tones a bit, I don''t know for sure.  To me the colours look right.<br/> <br/>I''m really not sure what to tell you.  I think it is a beautiful shot as it is, but it is not one that will stand out amongst 500 other shots.  I hope this helps.<br/> <br/>~Ursula</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club Strong points:  The light.  The light is very beautiful in this image, it''s what makes the image. Possible weaknesses:  It''s not all that interesting of a place (for a picture in a challenge I mean). Overall, I think this is a beautiful image, because of the light, but outside of that there isn''t much to hold anyone (except if you know the place and want to remember the good times you had there).  It''s a real pity you didn''t get more comments.  I don''t think the "distractions" are an issue here, but it is possible that a slightly different crop (or different position to make the image) would help. As for the post-processing, I think it is really quite adequate for the picture.  One possibility would be to intensify the red tones a bit, I don''t know for sure.  To me the colours look right. I''m really not sure what to tell you.  I think it is a beautiful shot as it is, but it is not one that will stand out amongst 500 other shots.  I hope this helps. ~Ursula', '2007-05-08 14:42:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(3628946, 505689, 2560, '<td valign="top">I entered this one instead of a waterfall picture because it made the wow page on P.Direct. I also had a version of this but more artsy that I liked better but I had to see how this would do.</td>', 'I entered this one instead of a waterfall picture because it made the wow page on P.Direct. I also had a version of this but more artsy that I liked better but I had to see how this would do.', '2007-05-08 14:46:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(3628947, 504935, 30982, '<td valign="top">The thing that gets my attention isn''t the car, it''s the guy to the right of the car.  He seems utterly uninterested in the spectacle.  The guy behind the car almost looks like he''s trying to undo a wedgie.  :-)  Given expert editing, maybe you could have deleted all the elements except the car, the red car behind, and the flags.  Then it would have been more DPC''ish.  And add the young lady to the hood of course.</td>', 'The thing that gets my attention isn''t the car, it''s the guy to the right of the car.  He seems utterly uninterested in the spectacle.  The guy behind the car almost looks like he''s trying to undo a wedgie.  :-)  Given expert editing, maybe you could have deleted all the elements except the car, the red car behind, and the flags.  Then it would have been more DPC''ish.  And add the young lady to the hood of course.', '2007-05-08 14:47:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(3628959, 501980, 11843, '<td valign="top">I don''t think I would have scored the photo as high without the buoys. They definitely add to the composition here even though they are somewhat ambiguous. I don''t think they hurt the overall effect. Again, Great work!</td>', 'I don''t think I would have scored the photo as high without the buoys. They definitely add to the composition here even though they are somewhat ambiguous. I don''t think they hurt the overall effect. Again, Great work!', '2007-05-08 14:51:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(3628978, 502970, 15291, '<td valign="top">Hi David,<br/>         A close-up head shot would have been awsome here with the flighing meat, the pinned ears and the meat hanging from the mouth. I have done this same thing countless times trying to capture the beauty of the entire animal when a head shot would have been better.</td>', 'Hi David,         A close-up head shot would have been awsome here with the flighing meat, the pinned ears and the meat hanging from the mouth. I have done this same thing countless times trying to capture the beauty of the entire animal when a head shot would have been better.', '2007-05-08 14:56:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(3628984, 504935, 63495, '<td valign="top">Jeb i didnt have time to vote on free study this time so i didnt vote on it. But i like the shot. I can see what some have commented that if you could have got more of a side profile shot and removed the guy it might have done better.But when you are shooting at events like this its not like shooting a model or a tree, You just have to take what you can get from where you are and i think the voters are so used to voteing on setup shots that we often forget it when looking at shot like this.<br/> <br/> I am planning on going to Topeka to the dragraces in june an i will be happy if i get anything close to this.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-05-08 13:58:46.</i></td>', 'Jeb i didnt have time to vote on free study this time so i didnt vote on it. But i like the shot. I can see what some have commented that if you could have got more of a side profile shot and removed the guy it might have done better.But when you are shooting at events like this its not like shooting a model or a tree, You just have to take what you can get from where you are and i think the voters are so used to voteing on setup shots that we often forget it when looking at shot like this.  I am planning on going to Topeka to the dragraces in june an i will be happy if i get anything close to this.', '2007-05-08 14:57:34.000000', '2007-05-08 14:58:46.000000', 0),
(3628986, 504935, 40973, '<td valign="top">Maybe if the young woman were naked - this could have gone into the nude gallery? Yes, I''m warped-just ignore me.</td>', 'Maybe if the young woman were naked - this could have gone into the nude gallery? Yes, I''m warped-just ignore me.', '2007-05-08 14:58:10.000000', NULL, 0),
