(3637184, 497999, 61679, '<td valign="top">Hello from the Critique Club,<br/> <br/>A very creative entry for a free study.  Most photographers equate images like this with a mistake they have made when taking an image (Oh crap, I forgot to reset my shutter speed).  Although when done intentionally for artistic purposes, most photographers think to themselves "That doesn''t take much skill, all they have to do is use long exposure time" or "Is that all they could come with".  Either way, the score will not be pretty, as you can attest.  Please continue experimenting and learning but be careful what you select for a free study.<br/> <br/>Feel free to PM me if you have any questions regarding this critique.<br/> <br/>Tim<br/></td>', 'Hello from the Critique Club, A very creative entry for a free study.  Most photographers equate images like this with a mistake they have made when taking an image (Oh crap, I forgot to reset my shutter speed).  Although when done intentionally for artistic purposes, most photographers think to themselves "That doesn''t take much skill, all they have to do is use long exposure time" or "Is that all they could come with".  Either way, the score will not be pretty, as you can attest.  Please continue experimenting and learning but be careful what you select for a free study. Feel free to PM me if you have any questions regarding this critique. Tim', '2007-05-10 14:18:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(3637195, 493871, 49934, '<td valign="top">Wow! Spectacularly impressive! Regards jnconradie</td>', 'Wow! Spectacularly impressive! Regards jnconradie', '2007-05-10 14:23:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(3637205, 495496, 4162, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the critique club:)<br/> <br/>Firstly I think that this is a very eye-catching shot. It has all the visual elements to keep the viewer looking including amazing sky detail which pulls the viewer to the barns, nice use of leading lines. <br/> <br/>I agree that the sky looks a little over-processed, but it has interesting colours and textures in it. <br/> <br/>I would really like to see this in black and white and very contrasty- I think it would be stunning.  Would it have been possible to get the sky detail over head and isolate one barn with the sky pulling the viewer in from above? <br/> <br/>Overall congrats on an excellent score and placing. <br/> <br/>Natasha<br/> <br/></td>', 'Greetings from the critique club:) Firstly I think that this is a very eye-catching shot. It has all the visual elements to keep the viewer looking including amazing sky detail which pulls the viewer to the barns, nice use of leading lines.  I agree that the sky looks a little over-processed, but it has interesting colours and textures in it.  I would really like to see this in black and white and very contrasty- I think it would be stunning.  Would it have been possible to get the sky detail over head and isolate one barn with the sky pulling the viewer in from above?  Overall congrats on an excellent score and placing.  Natasha ', '2007-05-10 14:28:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(3637209, 504789, 66348, '<td valign="top">LMAO... Love it.... You must have cooked him after takin him out and then bleached the heck out of the skeleton to get it that white. Not that I would know how to get the bones to look that great...</td>', 'LMAO... Love it.... You must have cooked him after takin him out and then bleached the heck out of the skeleton to get it that white. Not that I would know how to get the bones to look that great...', '2007-05-10 14:29:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(3637215, 500993, 62318, '<td valign="top">This is spectacular. The wonderful lines draw you across the frame. What really makes me like the photo is the boat, small details like that set this shot apart.</td>', 'This is spectacular. The wonderful lines draw you across the frame. What really makes me like the photo is the boat, small details like that set this shot apart.', '2007-05-10 14:31:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(3637227, 504550, 4162, '<td valign="top">Greeting from the critique club<br/> <br/>Firstly I am really surprised that this didnt''t score higher.. I thought it was very atmospheric.<br/> <br/>I think you have done a brilliant job at catching the mood of the performance..you can almost hear the music.  The lighting is fantastic and I love the way is catches the hair grip on the right and the mic also. Very cool!<br/> <br/>Focussing in such a hard lighting situation is good-the faces are very sharp with just some blurring on the body. Background detail is unseen which helps the singers really stand out. Great.<br/> <br/>You have said the biggest problem with the picture and that is that the mic is right in front of the girls face, I remember thinking this while voting. Perhaps if the girl was a little back from the mic it may have been possible to get her mouth and the mic... but you can hardly ask her to do this!  <br/> <br/>Overall i think this is a very good shot and I think you deserved to place a lot higher.<br/> <br/>Hope some of this helps<br/>Natasha</td>', 'Greeting from the critique club Firstly I am really surprised that this didnt''t score higher.. I thought it was very atmospheric. I think you have done a brilliant job at catching the mood of the performance..you can almost hear the music.  The lighting is fantastic and I love the way is catches the hair grip on the right and the mic also. Very cool! Focussing in such a hard lighting situation is good-the faces are very sharp with just some blurring on the body. Background detail is unseen which helps the singers really stand out. Great. You have said the biggest problem with the picture and that is that the mic is right in front of the girls face, I remember thinking this while voting. Perhaps if the girl was a little back from the mic it may have been possible to get her mouth and the mic... but you can hardly ask her to do this!   Overall i think this is a very good shot and I think you deserved to place a lot higher. Hope some of this helpsNatasha', '2007-05-10 14:36:53.000000', NULL, 0),
