(3643150, 504855, 10402, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/>What a cute kid! A great pose; he looks really natural and happy. I love the way he is peeking out from behind something. It''s a delightful portrait.<br/> <br/>Unfortunately, the flash is too bright and has washed out his face. There''s probably a way to set the intensity, although doing so quickly for a candid shot isn''t always feasible. A simple trick is to keep a plain white handkerchief handy to cover the flash when shooting at close range with just a moment''s notice. There''s probably no easy to recover from this in Photoshop (although you might try the Darken Shadows setting in the Shadows/Highlights tool).<br/> <br/>The black background works very well. It would be nicer if it was completely black, something easily done in most any photo editor. I''d also crop a bit off the bottom; there''s a bit too much space down there. (I personally think making the proportions 5x7 is about right.)<br/> <br/>Still, for a candid shot this turned out really well. I''m sure it''s a photo you''ll cherish for years.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club  What a cute kid! A great pose; he looks really natural and happy. I love the way he is peeking out from behind something. It''s a delightful portrait. Unfortunately, the flash is too bright and has washed out his face. There''s probably a way to set the intensity, although doing so quickly for a candid shot isn''t always feasible. A simple trick is to keep a plain white handkerchief handy to cover the flash when shooting at close range with just a moment''s notice. There''s probably no easy to recover from this in Photoshop (although you might try the Darken Shadows setting in the Shadows/Highlights tool). The black background works very well. It would be nicer if it was completely black, something easily done in most any photo editor. I''d also crop a bit off the bottom; there''s a bit too much space down there. (I personally think making the proportions 5x7 is about right.) Still, for a candid shot this turned out really well. I''m sure it''s a photo you''ll cherish for years.', '2007-05-12 23:40:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(3643330, 503876, 24111, '<td valign="top">Thank you for taking the time to comment!</td>', 'Thank you for taking the time to comment!', '2007-05-13 00:51:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(3643437, 503828, 37252, '<td valign="top">What a great shot! Perfect color tones. The focus and details well done. Love the pose and props</td>', 'What a great shot! Perfect color tones. The focus and details well done. Love the pose and props', '2007-05-13 01:22:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(3643785, 505205, 65547, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by MattO:</b></div><hr/><i> Greetings from the critique club. First off let me tell you this is a well done shot and I''m kind of suprised it didnt score higher then it did. I''m not sure most people understand the difficulty of shooting this type of photo. I''m really not sure what I can tell you to improve the shot. However I will tell you that adding a simple border does help with the voters and I might suggest that you try that next time. Overall well done. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thank you very much!<br/> <br/>Yes, I agree that most people don''t know even what it is on the picture. This kind of photography is pretty unknown but I found it very interesting and there''s a lot of beauty above us... Just we don''t know for it!<br/>Thank you also for advice for border. Will try this next time.<br/> <br/>You can also visit my web-page anytime. Thanks! ;)<br/> <br/>PrimozC</td>', 'Originally posted by MattO: Greetings from the critique club. First off let me tell you this is a well done shot and I''m kind of suprised it didnt score higher then it did. I''m not sure most people understand the difficulty of shooting this type of photo. I''m really not sure what I can tell you to improve the shot. However I will tell you that adding a simple border does help with the voters and I might suggest that you try that next time. Overall well done.   Thank you very much! Yes, I agree that most people don''t know even what it is on the picture. This kind of photography is pretty unknown but I found it very interesting and there''s a lot of beauty above us... Just we don''t know for it!Thank you also for advice for border. Will try this next time. You can also visit my web-page anytime. Thanks! ;) PrimozC', '2007-05-13 08:06:12.000000', NULL, 0),
