(4426437, 505471, 49804, '<td valign="top">Wow, my views have changed in the last 9 months of being on DPC, i came here thinking everything had to be a certain type of shot, and i actually gave this a 4 during voting. I came back to this today, and I thought "that is a really awesome shot." Really love the artsy feel to it, very unique shot which I like a lot, great job with the composition and lighting. Nicely done and I''m adding to faves.</td>', 'Wow, my views have changed in the last 9 months of being on DPC, i came here thinking everything had to be a certain type of shot, and i actually gave this a 4 during voting. I came back to this today, and I thought "that is a really awesome shot." Really love the artsy feel to it, very unique shot which I like a lot, great job with the composition and lighting. Nicely done and I''m adding to faves.', '2008-01-26 12:48:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(4428486, 505701, 34309, '<td valign="top">She is so perfect....<br/>Nice work capturing her beauty on the camera.</td>', 'She is so perfect....Nice work capturing her beauty on the camera.', '2008-01-27 10:50:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(4434292, 501058, 54228, '<td valign="top">Your post processing is top notch here, I''d be interested in how you did it.</td>', 'Your post processing is top notch here, I''d be interested in how you did it.', '2008-01-28 18:35:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(4442145, 497308, 34113, '<td valign="top">Wonderfully unique capture.</td>', 'Wonderfully unique capture.', '2008-01-30 22:50:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(4458452, 505471, 6519, '<td valign="top">Don''t feel like reading all the other comments, please forgive me if I repeat stuff.<br/> <br/>I love it! I can be pretty unforgiving with blur, too often I feel that an accidental blur is being passed off as "artistic". Not in this case - it feels very much intended and makes a wonderful contrast to the static architecture.<br/> <br/>I also love that you didn''t HDR the living daylights out of this - it feels so right to see very dark areas, as well as glimpses of light coming in.<br/> <br/>Saying that I don''t care for the blue back pack would be way too picky, so I won''t say it  :-)<br/> <br/>I just tried it in b+w - it looks good, too, but changes the mood quite a bit, so I''m glad you left those warm colors.</td>', 'Don''t feel like reading all the other comments, please forgive me if I repeat stuff. I love it! I can be pretty unforgiving with blur, too often I feel that an accidental blur is being passed off as "artistic". Not in this case - it feels very much intended and makes a wonderful contrast to the static architecture. I also love that you didn''t HDR the living daylights out of this - it feels so right to see very dark areas, as well as glimpses of light coming in. Saying that I don''t care for the blue back pack would be way too picky, so I won''t say it  :-) I just tried it in b+w - it looks good, too, but changes the mood quite a bit, so I''m glad you left those warm colors.', '2008-02-04 20:22:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(4460648, 505471, 16488, '<td valign="top">This image speaks to me about the relative permanence of the things we build versus our transient nature. We walk through our days and our lives in old halls whose enduring quality goes largely unquestioned not questioning our own mortality. Bravo!</td>', 'This image speaks to me about the relative permanence of the things we build versus our transient nature. We walk through our days and our lives in old halls whose enduring quality goes largely unquestioned not questioning our own mortality. Bravo!', '2008-02-05 15:54:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(4468323, 498589, 48954, '<td valign="top">picture of toys, when not for a toy challenge, tend to bomb. To be avoided in the future. However, It''s a great capture. Composition is great. love the lighting and the colors :)</td>', 'picture of toys, when not for a toy challenge, tend to bomb. To be avoided in the future. However, It''s a great capture. Composition is great. love the lighting and the colors :)', '2008-02-07 13:23:08.000000', NULL, 0);
